  "releaseNotes": "A predicate passed to GetAll filters instead of becoming a sort key.\n\n    Fixed:\n    - GetAll(x => x.IsActive) bound to the sorting overload with TProperty = bool, because the type parameter of the filter overload cannot be inferred. It returned every document, sorted by the predicate, without a warning. A new non-generic GetAll(filter, page, pageSize, session) takes the predicate, so the same call now filters.\n    - GetAllDescending(x => x.IsActive) had the same trap. A descending order needs a sorting expression, so the call is now a compile error (CS0619) pointing to GetAllDescending(filter, sorting).\n\n    Added:\n    - GetAll(filter, page, pageSize, session, cancellationToken): LINQ predicate with optional paging, no sort, session-aware.\n\n    Behaviour change:\n    - Code that used a bool lambda to sort now gets only the matching documents. To keep the sort, name the argument: GetAll(sorting: x => x.IsActive) and GetAllDescending(sorting: x => x.IsActive). An explicit type argument alone is ambiguous with the obsolete generic filter overloads until v13.\n    - The binding is decided at compile time: code compiled against 12.2.0 or earlier, including libraries built on this package, keeps the old behaviour until it is recompiled.\n    - A derived repository that overrides the generic GetAll(sorting) to add its own logic should override the new GetAll(filter) as well.\n    - IReadOnlyDataRepository has two new members with default implementations; classes implementing the interface directly compile and load unchanged.\n\n    See CHANGELOG.md for the full notes.",
